\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O Saviour, bless us ere we go;
\par Thy word into our minds instil;
\par And make our lukewarm hearts 
\par to glow
\par With lowly love and fervent will.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Through life's long day and death's
\par dark night,
\par O gentle Jesus, be our light.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The day is done, its hours have run,
\par And Thou hast taken count of all-
\par The scanty triumphs grace hath won,
\par The broken vow, the frequent fall.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Through life's long day and death's
\par dark night,
\par O gentle Jesus, be our light.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Grant us, dear Lord, from evil ways
\par True absolution and release;
\par And bless us, more than in past days,
\par With purity and inward peace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Through life's long day and death's
\par dark night,
\par O gentle Jesus, be our light.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Do more than pardon: give us joy,
\par Sweet fear and sober liberty,
\par And loving hearts without alloy
\par That only long to be like Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Through life's long day and death's
\par dark night,
\par O gentle Jesus, be our light.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. For all we love, the poor, the sad,
\par The sinful, unto Thee we call;
\par O let Thy mercy make us glad;
\par Thou art our Jesus and our all.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Through life's long day and death's
\par dark night,
\par O gentle Jesus, be our light.
\par                        Amen.\cf1\ul\b\f1\fs16 
\par 
\par }

